-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",67,{
[2113]="700270AE\n1\tTalk to Halbarad in Lhanuch\tHalbarad is in the centre of the village of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin. You have been told that Halbarad is assembling the Grey Company in preparation for its departure and should travel to Lhanuch for the last of the preparations before departing.\n2\tTalk to Braigiar in Lhanuch\030Talk to Prestadír in Lhanuch\tPrestadír and Braigiar, in the centre of Lhanuch, are considering the two paths the Grey Company will take to enter Dunland. Halbarad has asked you to consult with Prestadír and Braigiar about his proposed routes into Dunland.\n3\tTalk to Halbarad in Lhanuch\tHalbarad is in the centre of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin. You have spoken with Prestadír and Braigiar about the paths into Dunland.\n",
[2114]="700001E1\n1\tTalk to Elladan\tElladan is at his camp of Thorenhad on the north-western slope of the Bruinen Gorges, north of the bear-dens. Lord Elrond has asked you to lend your assistance to his sons Elladan and Elrohir, currently seeking the missing Nazgûl.\n",
[2115]="70027B09\n1\tTalk to Fâsh and go with him to see Saruman\tIn the caverns below Isengard, Fâsh is ready to bring you to Saruman.\n2\tTalk to Morflak in the Ring of Isengard\tAs it appears that you are still of some use to Saruman, you have survived your encounter with the Wizard. You have been deposited before Morflak, your new handler while within the ring of Isengard.\n",
[2116]="70027B13\n1\tComplete 'Their Best Interests' for Morflak's lackey\tMorflak has assigned one of his lackeys to keep an eye on you within the ring of Isengard and to give you work. If this Uruk-hai wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.\n2\tComplete 'Raiding the Larder' for Morflak's lackey\tMorflak has assigned one of his lackeys to keep an eye on you within the ring of Isengard and to give you work. If this Uruk-hai wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.\n3\tComplete 'Trivial Business' for Morflak's lackey\tMorflak has assigned one of his lackeys to keep an eye on you within the ring of Isengard and to give you work. If this Uruk-hai wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.\n4\tReturn to Morflak within the Ring of Isengard\tMorflak is waiting to speak with you within the ring of Isengard.\n",
[2117]="70027B1C\n1\tTalk to Fâsh in the Isengard Depths\tFâsh is in the caverns beneath Isengard, accessible by a door directly north of the tower. Once in the depths, you should take the sloping paths downward to Fâsh's command. Morflak has sent you to deliver a message to Fâsh and to do more work for him.\n2\tTalk to Barkh in the kitchens\tBarkh is in the kitchens beneath Isengard, south-west of the main cavern. Fâsh has sent you to help out in the kitchens once again.\n3\tClean up piles of slop in the kitchens (total: 6)\tThe floor of the kitchen is covered in slop. Barkh has given you a dirty rag and wants you to clean the slop up off the floor.\n4\tDulan has tried to catch your eye. Talk to him without attracting attention\tDulan in the kitchens has tried to catch your eye. You should talk to Dulan and see what he wants.\n5\tUruk-hai meals can be found on the tables in the kitchens below Isengard. Dulan has secretly given you a small quantity of poison and wants you to add it to one of the Uruk-hai meals.\t\n6\tClean up piles of slop in the kitchens (total: 6)\tSlop covers the floor of the kitchens below Isengard. Barkh wants you to clean up the slop.\n7\tUse the slop bucket in the kitchens to squeeze out the dirty rag\tIt is time for you to squeeze out the dirty rag into the slop bucket in the kitchens.\n8\tReturn the dirty rag to Barkh in the kitchens\tBarkh is in the kitchens below Isengard, south-west of the main cavern.\n9\tFill up a bucket of slop from the slop bucket in the kitchens\tBarkh wants you to fill a pan from the slop bucket in the kitchens and carry it to the bucket in the dungeons from where the prisoners are fed, as you did before.\n10\tTalk to Baldgar in the dungeon\tBaldgar wants to speak with you. He is in the dungeons below Isengard.\n",
[2118]="70027B1E\n1\tTalk to Acca in the dungeons\tAcca is in the dungeons below Isengard, located in the north-west corner of the main cavern.\n2\tTalk to Acca and experience 'Session: The Wizard's Vale' or read the shortened account instead\tAcca is imprisoned in the dungeons below Isengard. Acca, once the steward of Isengard, has agreed to tell you the story of his fall.\n3\tTalk to Acca in the dungeon\tAcca has told you the story of his fall and has warmed up to you. He is waiting to speak with you.\n4\tTalk to Baldgar in the dungeon\tBaldgar is in the dungeons below Isengard. Acca has agreed to help you escape and wants you to tell Baldgar.\n",
[2119]="70027B1F\n1\tTalk to Sagrúrz at the forge\tSagrúrz is by the forges in the main cavern beneath Isengard. Baldgar wants you to do the work Sagrúrz asks of you, but while you are doing that, he also wants you to collect some black powder.\n2\tCollect scattered weapons (total: 8)\030Collect piles of black powder (total: 4)\tWeapons are scattered around the floor near the forges. Sagrúrz wants you to pick them up and put them back in an empty barrel. Meanwhile, Baldgar wants you to collect some of the black powder that spews from the works and collects on the floor.\n3\tPut the scattered weapons in the empty barrel\tThe empty barrel is near the forges in the main cavern beneath Isengard. Sagrúrz wants you to put the scattered weapons you collected in an empty barrel.\n4\tTalk to Sagrúrz at the forge\tSagrúrz is waiting to speak with you by the forges in the main cavern beneath Isengard.\n5\tReturn to Baldgar with the stolen black powder\tBaldgar is in the dungeons below Isengard. You have stolen some black powder and should bring it to Baldgar.\n",
[2120]="70027B26\n1\tLeave the black powder near the largest of the war machines under construction. Keep sprinkling the powder until it is gone.\030Find the largest of the war-machines under construction within the Ring\tThe largest of the war-machines is being constructed on the surface, within the Ring of Isengard. The door to the surface is in the north wall of the caverns. The war-machines are south-east of the steps of Orthanc. Baldgar has asked you to leave the black powder that you collected near the largest of the war-machines under construction. You have enough black powder for four small piles.\n2\tLeave the black powder near the largest of the war-machines under construction\tYou have sprinkled the black powder near the largest of the war-machines under construction.\n3\tTalk to Thak\tThak is near the war-machines on the surface, within the Ring of Isengard. Thak noticed you lingering near the war-machines and has called you to speak with him.\n4\tTalk to Morflak\030Talk to Baldgar\tThak gave you some trouble when you went to leave the black powder at the war-machine. Now you can either speak to Morflak about Thak, as you threatened, or you can go directly back to Baldgar in the dungeons below Isengard. The door to the depths is north of Orthanc, and Morflak is south-west of the tower.\n5\tTalk to Baldgar in the dungeon\tBaldgar is in the dungeons below Isengard. The entrance to the depths is north of the tower of Orthanc. You have left the black powder near the largest of the war-machines within the Ring and should speak now with Baldgar in the dungeons.\n",
[2121]="70027B2D\n1\tTalk to Baldgar and carry out the escape plan\tBaldgar is in the dungeons below Isengard.\n2\tTalk to Baldgar in the Gravenwood\tWhen you awaken, you find that you have been carried to the Gravenwood, but Baldgar is near death.\n",
[2122]="70027B4A\n1\tFind Théodred at his camp in the Gravenwood and talk to him\tThéodred should be at his camp in the Gravenwood.\n",
[2123]="70027B4B\n1\tTalk to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp\030Talk to Seren at the Rohirrim scout-camp\030Talk to Hogawise at the Rohirrim scout-camp\tSaeradan, Seren, and Hogawise are at Théodred's camp in the Gravenwood. Théodred wants you to speak to survivors of the Falcon-clan's betrayal in order to learn what happened while you were imprisoned in Isengard.\n2\tTalk to Théodred at the Rohirrim scout-camp\tThéodred is at his camp in the Gravenwood.\n",
[2124]="70027B58\n1\tTravel into Tâl Methedras and find Théodred's forward encampment\tThéodred's men have formed a camp in sight of the lake in Tâl Methedras. You should go there to begin planning the rescue of the Grey Company.\n2\tTalk to Théodred at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras\tThéodred is waiting to speak with you at his forward encampment, in Tâl Methedras.\n3\tFrom his forward encampment in Tâl Methedras, Théodred makes preparations to launch an attack on Tûr Morva.\t\n4\tTalk to Théodred at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras\tThéodred is at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras. You have completed the necessary preparations and are now ready to attempt the rescue of the Grey Company from the prison-caves of Tûr Morva.\n",
[2125]="700270AF\n1\tTalk to Braigiar once you arrive at Dúvispont, in Dunland\tBraigiar will speak with you again just across the border of Enedwaith and Dunland, at Dúvispont, in Trum Dreng.\n2\tScout ahead and help an inhabitant of Trum Dreng\tThe plains of Trum Dreng lie to the south. Braigiar has asked you to scout Trum Dreng, keeping an eye out for its residents.\n3\tTalk to Braigiar in Lhan Tarren, the village of the Stag-clan\tBraigiar is waiting to speak with you just outside Lhan Tarren, the village of the Stag-clan. You should speak with Braigiar before proceeding.\n",
[2126]="70000FBF\n1\tFind some sign of the missing Nazgûl\030Use the Elf-stone to draw upon your inner inspiration\030If you find yourself without a full fellowship you may draw upon inspiration\tThe hoofprints were discovered far south of the road, and the sons of Elrond believe that the missing Rider might be hiding in the ruins of Minas Agor, located within the narrow channels of the South Trollshaws. Elladan has asked you to follow the Nazgûl into the South Trollshaws. The Elf-stone can be used to allow for you to access the inspiration buff while solo or in a smaller fellowship.\n2\tRemove bridle from the black horse's corpse\030Use the Elf-stone to draw upon your inner inspiration\030If you find yourself without a full fellowship you may draw upon inspiration\tThe corpse of a black horse lies in the ruins of Minas Agor, located among the narrow channels of the South Trollshaws. You should remove the bridle from the horse's corpse and return with it to Elladan. The Elf-stone can be used to allow for you to access the inspiration buff while solo or in a smaller fellowship.\n3\tBring bridle of the black steed to Elladan\tElladan is at Thorenhad, located among the Bruinen Gorges, north of a bear-den. Elladan will be both pleased and troubled to see the bridle of the black horse, for it means that the missing Rider is still somewhere within the Trollshaws.\n",
[2127]="700270B7\n1\tTalk to Prestadír just inside the entrance of the Bonevales, west of the road from Enedwaith\tPrestadír will speak with you again just across the border of Enedwaith and Dunland, in the Bonevales, west of the road.\n2\tHelp Bledhun and his friends, then meet Prestadír at the hidden valley\tPrestadír has asked you to scout the Bonevales and learn what threats may lie in wait here and to help Bledhun and his friends.\n3\tTalk to Prestadír at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales\tPrestadír is waiting to speak with you at the camp he established in a hidden valley in the Bonevales.\n",
[2128]="7004426D\n1\tMount your steed and talk to Derufin outside the Causeway Forts to begin the ride to Minas Tirith\tDerufin is outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern end of the Pelennor Fields. Duilin and Derufin are ready to climb aboard their steeds and ride to Minas Tirith. They wait only for your word that you are ready to do the same.\n2\tTalk to Prince Imrahil just inside the entrance to Minas Tirith\tPrince Imrahil has dismounted from his steed just inside the gates of Minas Tirith, on the western end of the Pelennor Fields. You helped save Faramir from death at the hands of the Orcs, but he is grievously wounded. Prince Imrahil of Dol Amroth has borne him back to the city, and wishes to speak with you.\n3\tTalk to Gandalf just inside the entrance to Minas Tirith\tGandalf can be found just within the gates to Minas Tirith. Faramir has suffered an unnatural wound during the retreat from the Causeway Forts, and Gandalf bears a concerned expression.\n",
[2129]="70027B7A\n1\tTalk to Théodred and begin the attack on the prison-caves\tThéodred is at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras. Théodred is waiting to speak with you about beginning the attack on the prison-caves where the Grey Company is being held.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad at the Rohirrim scout-camp\tHalbarad is at Théodred's camp in the Gravenwood. You have come alive out of the prison-caves, along with Halbarad and some other surviving members of the Grey Company.\n",
[2130]="700270B6\n1\tHelp the people of Trum Dreng as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Halbarad in Pren Gwydh\tThere are many things you can do in Trum Dreng to aid the Stag-clan and gain their favour. Once you have satisfied their needs, Braigiar would like you to meet up with Halbarad outside the village of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh.\n",
[2131]="700270C2\n1\tHelp the people of the Bonevales as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Halbarad in Pren Gwydh\tThere are many things that you can do in the Bonevales to aid its people and gain their favour. Once you have satisfied their needs, Prestadír would like you to travel south into Pren Gwydh to meet up with Halbarad.\n",
[2132]="70044272\n1\tTalk to Thalgam at the Sword-gate to the Second Circle\tThalgam guards the Sword-gate to the Second Circle of Minas Tirith. Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.\n2\tTalk to Soromar at the Silver Gate to the Third Circle\tSoromar guards the Silver Gate to the Third Circle of Minas Tirith. Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.\n3\tTalk to Idhir at the Lords' Gate to the Fourth Circle\tIdhir guards the Lords' Gate to the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith. Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.\n4\tTalk to Doronir at the Gate of Stars to the Fifth Circle\tDoronir guards the Gate of Stars to the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith. Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.\n5\tTalk to Garthor at the Gate of Stones to the Sixth Circle\tGarthor guards the Gate of Stones to the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith. Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.\n6\tTalk to Linharn at the Gate of the Citadel to the Seventh Circle\tLinharn guards the Gate of the Citadel of Minas Tirith. Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.\n7\tTalk to Mithrandir in the Court of the Fountain, in the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith\tMithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain on the uppermost level of the city. You have obtained pass-words for the seven levels of Minas Tirith, and should now talk to Mithrandir in the Seventh Circle.\n",
[2133]="70001101\n1\tTalk to Glorfindel\tLord Glorfindel can be found in Imladris, far to the east of Thorenhad, contemplating the waterfalls by the Last Homely House. Elladan has asked you to consult with the Elf-lord Glorfindel about the missing Rider.\n2\tUse Glorfindel's beryl at the Ford of Bruinen\tThe Ford of Bruinen is to the west of Imladris, at the bottom of the steeply-climbing slopes. Lord Glorfindel has given you a beryl and has asked you to test its powers by holding it aloft on the banks of the Bruinen.\n3\tBring Glorfindel's beryl to Lord Glorfindel\tLord Glorfindel is in Imladris, high above the Bruinen and to the east, by the waterfall outside the Last Homely House. Glorfindel is waiting to speak with you upon your return from the Ford of Bruinen.\n",
[2134]="70001102\n1\tBring Glorfindel's beryl to Elladan\tElladan is at Thorenhad, his camp among the Bruinen Gorges, north of the bear-dens. Lord Glorfindel has sent you back to Elladan with a beryl, an Elf-stone that glows when it comes near places on which great evil has left its mark.\n",
[2135]="700270C3\n1\tFind someone in Galtrev who will share information with you\tHalbarad wants you to talk to the residents of Galtrev in order to learn of the situation in Pren Gwydh.\n2\tTalk to Catrin in Galtrev\tCatrin is in the village of Galtrev. You have been told to speak with Catrin.\n3\tTalk to Dai, Hulun, or Idwal\tCatrin has directed you to speak with Dai, Hulun, or Idwal in Galtrev.\n4\tTalk to Catrin in Galtrev\tCatrin is in Galtrev. You should speak with Catrin again.\n",
[2136]="70044281\n1\tTalk to Othnar and complete 'The Council of Gondor'\030Talk to Peregrin Took and complete 'Guard of the Citadel'\030Talk to Duilin and complete 'In Need of Discipline'\tThe Council of Gondor meets in the Dome of the Sun on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith. Peregrin Took can be found somewhere in the Citadel. Duilin and Derufin can be found within one of the taverns in the lower circles of the city. Mithrandir has asked you to provide help to a number of people within the city before the city is besieged.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir in the Court of the Fountain\tMithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain on the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith. You have aided the Council of Gondor, Peregrin Took, and the sons of Lord Duinhir of Blackroot Vale, and should now return to Mithrandir.\n3\tTalk to Imrahil in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, by the main gate to the city\tPrince Imrahil is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, by the main gate of the city, looking for someone to undertake a dangerous mission.\n",
[2137]="7004428E\n1\tTalk to Ingold at the North-gate in the Rammas Echor\tIngold is the Captain of the Out-wall, and can be found at the North-gate in the Rammas Echor. Prince Imrahil has asked you to learn why Ingold has not yet returned to Minas Tirith, and to learn the situation in Talath Anor.\n2\tDefeat Sûhalar Easterlings in Talath Anor (total: 8)\tSûhalar Easterlings can be found throughout the plains of Talath Anor, in Old Anórien. Ingold, Captain of the Out-wall, has asked you to defeat Sûhalar Easterlings throughout Talath Anor.\n3\tTalk to Barathant in Crithost\tIf he still lives, Barathant should be somewhere within the town of Crithost, in Talath Anor. Ingold asked you to find Barathant after you defeated some of the Sûhalar Easterlings.\n4\tDefeat Wargs or Warg-riders in Talath Anor (total: 4)\tWarg-riders can be found throughout Talath Anor. Barathant has asked you to defeat the Warg-riders that have overrun the lands north of the Rammas Echor.\n5\tTalk to Barathant in Crithost\tBarathant is in the town of Crithost, in Talath Anor. You defeated many foes and should now return to Crithost.\n",
[2138]="700270C4\n1\tCollect lumber-axes from the camp north-east of Galtrev (total: 8)\tThe lumber-camp in Pren Gwydh is north-east of Galtrev. Catrin has asked you to steal axes at the lumber-camp or from other hostile Dunlendings throughout Pren Gwydh, then throw the axes in a pond east of the camp.\n2\tThrow the bundle of axes into the pond\030Find the pond in which to throw the lumber axes\tThe pond where Catrin wanted you to throw the lumber-axes is east of the lumber-camp. Catrin asked you to steal lumber-axes from the camp north-east of Galtrev and throw them into the pond east of the camp.\n3\tCheck this stage in the quest journal.\t\n4\tTalk to Catrin at Galtrev\tCatrin is in the lower village of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh. Catrin will be pleased to hear that you have disrupted work at the lumber-camp.\n5\tLumber-piles can be found in the upper village of Galtrev. Catrin in the lower village of Galtrev has a torch for you to carry to lumber-piles throughout the upper village.\t\n6\tTalk to Catrin in Galtrev\tCatrin is in the lower village of Galtrev. You have burned wood-piles throughout the upper village and should return now to Catrin.\n",
[2139]="70001103\n1\tUse Glorfindel's beryl\030Find the deepest chamber of Torogrod\030Find the deepest chamber of Nurath\030Find the deepest chamber of Thingroth\030If you are not in a fellowship you can use the Shimmering Elf-stone to invoke inspiration\030If not in a fellowship you can use the Shimmering Elf-stone to invoke inspiration\tElladan gave you his notes containing the locations of the troll-caves. Elladan wants you to search three troll-caves with Glorfindel's beryl. Using the Shimmering Elf-stone allows you to access the inspiration buff while solo or in a smaller fellowship.\n2\tTalk to Elladan\030Collect Glorfindel's beryl\030Collect Elladan's Notes\030Collect Shimmering Elf-stone\tElladan is at Thorenhad, his camp among the Bruinen Gorges, north of the bear-dens. Elladan is waiting to hear what Glorfindel's beryl revealed: that the missing Nazgûl was never in any of the caves you searched.\n",
[2140]="70000FC5\n1\tTalk to Barachen\tBarachen is at his camp south of the Great East Road that runs through the South Trollshaws. Scouts along the road can direct you to him. Elladan told you that Barachen reported seeing one of the Onodrim somewhere in the wild and wants you to talk to him about it.\n2\tFind the Onod\tOne of the Onodrim, a creature of ancient days, was seen in the valley of the giants south of the High Moor, high above the Bruinen. Barachen reportedly saw the Onod standing next to some mighty trees as he came south into the valley. Barachen reported seeing one of the Onodrim somewhere in the Trollshaws, and Elladan thinks it possible that this Onod might know something of the missing Nazgûl's whereabouts.\n3\tTalk to Elladan\tElladan is at Thorenhad, his camp among the Bruinen Gorges, north of the bear-dens. Elladan will be troubled to learn the fate of the Onod that Barachen saw in the valley of the giants.\n",
[2141]="70044292\n1\tFind Cangrail and tell her to return\030Find Brúnion and tell him to return\030Defeat foes throughout Talath Anor (total: 8)\tCangrail and Brúnion can be found to the north-west and north-east of Crithost, in Talath Anor. Barathant asked you to find and recall the scout he sent out from Crithost, and to defeat any enemies you come across in Talath Anor.\n2\tTalk to Barathant in Crithost\tBarathant is in the town of Crithost, waiting to hear that his scouts have agreed to return to the North-gate of the Rammas Echor.\n3\tTalk to Ingold at the North-gate of the Rammas Echor\tIngold, the Captain of the Out-wall, is at the North-gate of the Rammas Echor. The scouts in Talath Anor are retreating to the North-gate, and you should do the same. Ingold is waiting for your return.\n4\tWait for Barathant at the North-gate of the Rammas Echor\tBarathant never returned to the North-gate, but Ingold cannot wait long for him.\n5\tTalk to Ingold at the North-gate of the Rammas Echor\tIngold, the Captain of the Out-wall, is at the North-gate of the Rammas Echor.\n6\tRetreat to Minas Tirith and talk to Imrahil in the First Circle of the city\tPrince Imrahil is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, waiting for you to return with news of the situation in Talath Anor.\n",
[2142]="700272DA\n1\tAid the people of Pren Gwydh as much as you can before moving on to Tâl Methedras\tTûr Morva is in Tâl Methedras, to the east of Pren Gwydh. Catrin has asked you to aid the people of Galtrev and Pren Gwydh as much as you can before moving on to Tâl Methedras.\n2\tTalk to Léolin, and he will bring you to Tûr Morva\tLéolin is suspicious of you, but has agreed to bring you to meet Lheu Brenin. You have met the guard at the pass into Tâl Methedras, but he is wary of you and the Rangers. He is waiting to travel with you to Tûr Morva.\n3\tTalk to Penrod in Tûr Morva\tPenrod is waiting to speak with you in Tûr Morva.\n",
[2143]="7002737F\n1\tEach member of the Falcon-clan in Tûr Morva has a task to do to prepare for battle against Saruman. Penrod has asked you to aid them with their tasks.\t\n2\tTalk to Penrod in Tûr Morva\tPenrod will be glad to hear that you have aided the people of Tûr Morva with their preparations.\n3\tTalk to Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva\tLheu Brenin is outside his home, up the hill to the south of Penrod, in Tûr Morva. Penrod has told you that the Brenin wants to see you concerning some trouble with the captive emissary of Isengard.\n",
[2144]="70044295\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir and complete 'A Matter of Lineage'\030Talk to Arodor and complete 'A Long Siege'\030Talk to Echadon and complete 'Reserves of Courage'\tThe Council of Gondor meets in the Dome of the Sun on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith. Mithrandir can be found at the Court of the Fountain, in the Citadel atop the city. Echadon can be found at the south end of the Second Circle. Imrahil has asked you to provide help to a number of people within the city before the city is encircled by a ring of foes.\n2\tTalk to Imrahil in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, by the main gate to the city\tPrince Imrahil is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, by the main gate of the city, preparing for battle.\n3\tTalk to Ormatar in the Citadel atop Minas Tirith\tOrmatar is in the Citadel, the highest level of Minas Tirith. You learned that Ormatar has been seeking you, and you should find out what he wants.\n",
})
